<Wiki
  title="puv package"
  description="Write dist/ as a PHAR, a zip, or a tar of the application and its dependencies."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>package</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv package</code> writes <code>dist/</code>. The archive contains the application and
    its dependencies. The PHP runtime stays outside. puv does not embed the runtime inside a PHAR.
  </p>

  <h2>The manifest format</h2>
  <pre class="block">[package]
format = "phar"
entrypoint = "src/main.php"</pre>
  <pre class="block">puv package</pre>
  <p>
    <code>format</code> and <code>entrypoint</code> come from <code>[package]</code>. That table
    is on <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>A format for one run</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv package --format phar
puv package --format zip
puv package --format tar</pre>
  <p>
    <code>--format</code> is <code>phar</code>, <code>zip</code>, or <code>tar</code>. It selects
    the archive for this invocation. The runtime stays outside all three.
  </p>

  <h2>Build versus package</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/wiki/commands/build"><code>puv build</code></a> runs the <code>build</code> script
    when you declared one, and writes <code>dist/</code> only when you did not.
    <code>puv package</code> is the command whose job is <code>dist/</code>, with an explicit
    format.
  </p>
</Wiki>
